{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Patel. I understand you came in because you’ve been hearing voices about your baby?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… they keep saying something bad is going to happen. I got really scared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry you’re going through that. But I want you to know we’re here to help. The baby’s heart rate looks good, and you’re not having any contractions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I called my OB earlier because I felt less movement, but then it got back to normal. I just started hearing these voices after that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. The decrease in movement worried you, and that may have triggered some anxiety. But fetal monitoring shows your baby is doing well now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t feel like I’m losing touch with reality, but the voices are so loud. They don’t tell me to hurt anyone, just that the baby is in danger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you for sharing that. It sounds like a symptom of your bipolar disorder, possibly a peripartum psychosis. The psychiatry team will be coming to see you shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been through this before. I had ECT during this pregnancy already. I just didn’t take my Haldol today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see that. You were on Haldol 1mg twice a day, right? Skipping it might have contributed to this episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I should’ve taken it. I just felt okay this morning and thought I could manage without it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "These episodes can come on quickly, especially during pregnancy. We’re going to restart your Haldol and adjust the dose with the psychiatry team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help the voices go away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should, over the next day or two. They may also give you some Ativan to help with the agitation and help you rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m also feeling kind of weak. And my heart is racing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your heart rate is a bit high, and your blood pressure is on the lower side. We checked your labs — your white blood cell count is elevated, and your bicarbonate is low, which suggests some dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t eaten much. I’ve been too anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. We’ll start you on IV fluids to help with the dehydration and get some nutrition in you. We also want to make sure your asthma and reflux are managed — you’re on ranitidine, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I take that twice a day. My asthma has been okay, just occasional use of my inhaler."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep monitoring that. For now, let’s get your IV started and let the psychiatry team evaluate you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The psychiatry team saw you earlier. They agree this is a manic episode with psychotic features. They’ve increased your Haldol to 2mg twice a day and added lorazepam as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I took the lorazepam last night. It helped me sleep a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. The goal is to reduce the voices and keep you calm. They also want to continue your Buspar for longer-term mood stability."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to stay here the whole pregnancy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, but because of your history of suicide attempts, even though you’re not having those thoughts now, they feel you need a higher level of psychiatric care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So… am I being transferred?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Once a bed opens up at a psychiatric facility that can care for pregnant women, you’ll be transferred there for ongoing treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared. What if something happens to the baby while I’m there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-01-22 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But the facility has experience with pregnant patients. You’ll continue prenatal care, and they’ll monitor the baby just like we are."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The voices are quieter. I still hear them, but not as loud. And I slept better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. Your vital signs are stable now, and your labs are improving. The dehydration is resolving with the IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I eat regular food now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve advanced your diet. Just take it slow. And keep taking your ranitidine for the reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my prenatal vitamins?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please continue those. They’re important for you and the baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The psychiatric facility has a bed for you. You’ll be transferred later today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What meds will I be on there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue Buspirone twice a day, Haldol — now 2mg in the morning, 2mg at 2 PM, and 4mg at bedtime — and lorazepam 1mg at night. Plus prenatal vitamins and ranitidine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a lot, but I’ll do it. I want to get better for my baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing the right thing. They’ll help you adjust the meds and stay safe. Your baby is doing well, and we’ll make sure your OB team stays involved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was really scared when this started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. But you reached out, and that was the most important step. You’re strong, and you’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team is here. Just a final check — you’re alert, your baby’s heart rate is strong, and you’re walking fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. Nervous, but ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely normal. We’ll send all your records over, and your OB will follow up with the facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I call you if I have questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can reach your OB team anytime. And the psychiatry team at the facility will be your main point of contact now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take care, and we’ll be checking in with your OB to make sure everything stays on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep taking my meds. I want to be healthy for my baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best plan. You’re doing great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think I’m ready to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright. The team will take you now. Wishing you all the best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll be rooting for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll stay in touch with my doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we can ask. You’re doing the right thing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And that’s a powerful place to be. Keep that hope alive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-01-24 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-01-22 08:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-01-24 15:54:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A pregnant patient with a history of bipolar disorder and prior psychiatric hospitalizations was admitted due to auditory hallucinations expressing fears about her baby's safety, consistent with a manic episode with psychotic features. She had no obstetric complications, and fetal monitoring remained reassuring throughout. She was restarted on haloperidol and lorazepam for agitation, with improvement in symptoms. Dehydration was identified and treated with IV fluids. Given her psychiatric history and ongoing risk, she was stabilized and transferred to an inpatient psychiatric facility for continued care. Her asthma and GERD were managed with routine medications, and she was discharged on a revised antipsychotic regimen with close follow-up planned.",
    "problems": [
      "Mental disorders of mother, antepartum condition or complication",
      "Bipolar I disorder, most recent episode (or current) depressed, severe, specified as with psychotic behavior",
      "Dehydration",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other current conditions classifiable elsewhere of mother, antepartum condition or complication"
    ]
  }
}
